course: dictionary
lesson: 2728
title: Diplomacy: talking instead of fighting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Diplomacy is a noun with two meanings: the work of governments talking to each other to keep peace and sort out problems, and the skill of dealing with people politely and carefully so that nobody gets upset. The sentence gives you a clue: «Most quarrels between countries are settled by diplomacy, which means talking and making deals.» The words after the comma explain the word for you.
explain: Use the swap check. Put «talking and making deals» in place of diplomacy in «Thailand kept its freedom by clever diplomacy». It still makes sense, so your meaning is right: Thailand kept its freedom by clever talks and deals.
explain: The everyday meaning is the same skill on a small scale. If a friend tells you something hard in a kind, careful way, you can say they used diplomacy. It is another word for tact.
fact: Diplomacy is an uncountable noun, so you say «a lot of diplomacy», not «a diplomacy».
fact: Useful phrases are «use diplomacy», «through diplomacy» and «diplomacy failed».
fact: «Diplomacy» means talking and making deals so that countries settle quarrels without fighting.
fact: «Public diplomacy» can mean government messages aimed at foreigners, meant to make people think well of a country.
fact: In the Amarna letters, from about 1350 BCE, kings of Egypt and Babylon called each other «brother» and asked for gold and gifts. Real diplomacy has always used letters, gifts and envoys.
exercise: «Most quarrels between countries are settled by diplomacy.» What does diplomacy mean here? | Writing secret letters to nobody | Fighting in a war | *Talking and making deals | Playing games on holiday
exercise: «He used diplomacy to tell his friend the truth without hurting her feelings.» What does diplomacy mean? | Keeping a secret | Shouting the truth loudly | Running away from problems | *Skill in being polite and careful so nobody gets upset
exercise: Find the word in «Real diplomacy used letters, gifts, envoys and royal marriages» that means messengers sent between countries. | gifts | letters | *envoys | marriages
test: «Thailand kept its freedom by clever diplomacy (careful talks and deals).» Why did Thailand keep its freedom? | Because it never had any neighbours | Because it was ruled by a king from Europe | *Because of careful talks and deals | Because it had the biggest army in Asia
test: Ben tells his brother gently that his model is broken, not rudely. Which word best describes what Ben used? | Anger | Shouting | *Diplomacy | Boasting
exam: What is diplomacy? | A sport played with paddles and a small ball | Loud shouting between two countries | *Careful talking and deals to keep peace, or polite skill that stops people getting upset | A map of old kingdoms
